---
import Flow from "../../components/Flow.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { research } from "../../content";

const item = research.find((entry) => entry.id === "agentic-data-transfer-optimizer");
if (!item) throw new Error("Agentic Data Transfer Optimizer content is missing");
---

<BaseLayout title="Agentic Data Transfer Optimizer · Nieb Hasan Neom" description={item.tagline} current="Research" compact>
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/#research">← Research</a></p>
    <header class="doc-head">
      <h1>{item.title}</h1>
      <p class="lede">{item.tagline}</p>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Status</dt><dd class:list={["status", `tone-${item.tone}`]}>{item.status}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Built with</dt><dd>{item.stack.join(", ")}</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p>
        Bulk data movers usually run with a hand-tuned, static concurrency setting. The right number of parallel streams depends on the network path, competing traffic, and host load, all of which change during a long transfer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        A sender and receiver move data over TCP through a multiprocessing worker pool with zero-copy <code>sendfile()</code> transfers. At each probing interval the system observes the transfer, two agents reason about it, and the runtime acts on a bounded recommendation.
      </p>
      <Flow
        label="Optimizer control loop"
        steps={[
          { title: "Observe", text: "Read TCP socket statistics, congestion window, retransmissions, RTT variance, and host load." },
          { title: "Diagnose", text: "The Diagnostic agent turns observations and recent history into a structured assessment." },
          { title: "Decide", text: "The Decision agent recommends a concurrency change or holds the current setting." },
          { title: "Enforce", text: "Hard limits, bounded deltas, graduated ramping, and oscillation damping shape the action." },
        ]}
        loop="Each action is evaluated at the next interval, closing an observe, reason, act, evaluate loop."
      />
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Design choices</h2>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>The model recommends and the system enforces. No agent output can push concurrency outside the permitted range.</li>
        <li>Repeated reversals are detected and damped before the next action, and large changes are ramped in steps.</li>
        <li>Structured memory and a decision journal record what each agent saw and chose.</li>
        <li>The model layer is pluggable across local Ollama models, fine-tuned Hugging Face checkpoints, OpenAI, and Google Gemini.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Open questions</h2>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>Can agent decisions stay stable as telemetry changes, without oscillating?</li>
        <li>When does adaptive concurrency beat a well-chosen static setting, on which paths and workloads?</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The prototype is built and evaluation is under way. Results will appear here once controlled comparisons are complete.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
